# Copy to `.env.local` (gitignored) to override the backend the dev server talks
# to. Create React App only exposes vars prefixed with REACT_APP_, and only
# reads this file at startup — restart `npm start` after changing it.

# --- Which backend handles OAuth ---
# Unset (default): `npm start` talks to the local Express server on
#   http://127.0.0.1:8888, which needs your own SPOTIFY_ID / SPOTIFY_SECRET in
#   local-server/.env and http://127.0.0.1:8888/callback registered on the
#   Spotify app.
#
# Set to the deployed backend: sign in against the real Heroku app instead, so
#   you need NO Spotify credentials locally and NO extra redirect URI — the
#   OAuth round-trip uses the backend's own registered callback and only the
#   final hop comes back to localhost:3000. The backend only hands tokens back
#   to allowlisted origins (see RETURN_TARGETS in local-server/index.js).
# REACT_APP_BACKEND=https://key-track2.herokuapp.com
